.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/argparse Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
\fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
CLI arguments parser for node\&.js, with \fRsub-commands\fP support\&. Port of python's \fRargparse\fP (version \fR3\&.9\&.0\fP)\&.

.PP
\fBDifference with original\&.\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
JS has no keyword arguments support\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Pass options instead: \fRnew ArgumentParser({ description: 'example', add_help: true })\fP\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
JS has no python's types \fRint\fP, \fRfloat\fP, \&.\&.\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Use string-typed names: \fR\&.add_argument('-b', { type: 'int', help: 'help' })\fP\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRr\fP format specifier uses \fRrequire('util')\&.inspect()\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
More details in \fRdoc\fP\&.
.SH "Example"
.PP
\fRtest\&.js\fP file:

.PP
.PP
.nf
#!/usr/bin/env node
'use strict';

const { ArgumentParser } = require('argparse');
const { version } = require('\&./package\&.json');

const parser = new ArgumentParser({
  description: 'Argparse example'
});

parser\&.add_argument('\-v', '\-\-version', { action: 'version', version });
parser\&.add_argument('\-f', '\-\-foo', { help: 'foo bar' });
parser\&.add_argument('\-b', '\-\-bar', { help: 'bar foo' });
parser\&.add_argument('\-\-baz', { help: 'baz bar' });

console\&.dir(parser\&.parse_args());
.fi
.PP

.PP
Display help:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ \&./test\&.js \-h
usage: test\&.js [\-h] [\-v] [\-f FOO] [\-b BAR] [\-\-baz BAZ]

Argparse example

optional arguments:
  \-h, \-\-help         show this help message and exit
  \-v, \-\-version      show program's version number and exit
  \-f FOO, \-\-foo FOO  foo bar
  \-b BAR, \-\-bar BAR  bar foo
  \-\-baz BAZ          baz bar
.fi
.PP

.PP
Parse arguments:

.PP
.PP
.nf
$ \&./test\&.js \-f=3 \-\-bar=4 \-\-baz 5
{ foo: '3', bar: '4', baz: '5' }
.fi
.PP
